#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
colibrì — tiny engine, immense model.
Run GLM-5.2 (744B) locally on CPU with roughly 15-26 GB of RAM.

  qwanto chat               interactive chat (loads the model once)
  qwanto serve              OpenAI-compatible HTTP API (persistent engine)
  qwanto run "prompt"       one-shot generation
  qwanto info               model, RAM, disk, and configuration status
  qwanto plan               Disk / RAM / VRAM resource plan
  qwanto doctor             installation and execution-plan diagnostics
  qwanto bench [task...]    quality benchmarks (MMLU/HellaSwag/...)
  qwanto convert            convert GLM-5.2-FP8 to int4, one shard at a time
  qwanto pack               convert safetensors to Qwanto Native .qwn
  qwanto inspect            inspect a Qwanto Native .qwn file
  qwanto build              build the engine

Configuration through environment variables or flags (also valid after the subcommand):
  QWANTO_MODEL=<dir>   model directory (default /home/vincenzo/glm52_i4)
  --ram N            RAM budget in GB (automatically sizes the expert cache)
  --repin N          adapt RAM/VRAM experts every N tokens
  --topp P           adaptive expert top-p             --topk N   fixed top-k
  --ngen N           maximum response tokens           --cap N    cache slots/layer
"""
